Description: Determine the minimal set of proteins that explains the peptide
    spectrum matches (PSMs) of a mass spectrometry experiment, using a greedy
    parsimony algorithm. Annotate peptides with the proteins they match in
    'FASTA' sequence databases, and create 'FASTA' databases with reversed
    decoy sequences and contaminant proteins. Estimate the false discovery
    rate (FDR) of target-decoy search results at the PSM, precursor, peptide
    and protein level, following Elias and Gygi (2007) <doi:10.1038/nmeth1019>
    and Käll et al. (2008) <doi:10.1021/pr700600n>. Compute variable precursor
    isolation windows for data-independent acquisition (DIA) from the
    distribution of precursor (MS1) masses.
